SUMMARY:Edible & Medicinal Plant Walk
DESCRIPTION:Join Certified California Naturalist Mary Good on a hike exploring the medicinal and edible plants of the park. Weaving in natural history\, ethnobotany\, herbalism and folktales\, this walk will open your senses\, as well as your curiosity to the abundance of plantlore in Sonoma County. \nTickets are $15 for adults\, $7.5 for youth (12-17 year olds)\, students\, Sugarloaf members\, and Sugarloaf or RFO volunteers\, and free for children under 12. Tickets day-of on site will be $20 and might not be available. All children under 18 must be accompanied by a parent or legal guardian. Meet at the White Barn parking lot. Bring at least a quart of water and a lunch and be prepared for a leisurely 2-3 mile walk with a 250-ft climb. Wear layers\, appropriate footwear for slippery (and possibly muddy) terrain\, and sun protection. Heavy rains cancel; parking fees apply.
URL:https://golocal.coop/event/edible-medicinal-plant-walk-2/
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park\, 2605 Adobe Canyon Rd\, Kenwood\, CA
CATEGORIES:Recreation
GEO:38.4427;-122.533
