SUMMARY:Living History Day
DESCRIPTION:Meet the vaqueros\, traders\, cooks\, and crafts people who lived in Alta California. Join us for blacksmithing and woodworking demonstrations. Bring a picnic and play historical games! Junior Rangers: Bring your logbooks to earn a badge and stamp! Admission includes activities: Adults $3.00\, Children 6 to 17 $2.00\, Children 5 and under free! \nCalifornia State Parks supports equal access. Prior to arrival\, visitors with disabilities who need\nassistance should contact: Petaluma Adobe SHP (707) 762 – 4871.
URL:https://golocal.coop/event/living-history-day/
LOCATION:Petaluma Adobe State Historic Park\, 3325 Adobe Road\, Petaluma\, CA
CATEGORIES:Kids and Family,Other,Recreation
